<title>USA: Stratosphere says bankruptcy likely.</title>
<headline>Stratosphere says bankruptcy likely.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stratosphere Corp., operator of the Stratosphere hotel-casino in Las Vegas, said Thurdsay it does not plan to make an interest payment due next month on mortgage notes and will probably file bankruptcy.</p>
<p>Stratosphere, which has struggled since opening on April 30, is currently negotiating with creditors to amend terms of its $203 million of 14.25 percent first mortgage notes.</p>
<p>&quot;It is highly likely that negotations with its creditors, whether successful or not at arriving at a restructuring, will involve a bankruptcy filing,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Grand Casinos Inc., which owns and operates hotel-casino properties in several states, owns 42 percent of Stratosphere.</p>
